From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:33:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] payloads/edk2: Only select the serial console with a UART
 driver

EDK2_DEBUG and EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT select CONSOLE_SERIAL, which
depends on DRIVERS_UART. On boards without a UART driver, e.g.
lenovo/w541, either option leaves CONSOLE_SERIAL with unmet
dependencies and the build stops in olddefconfig. Configs that had
EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT enabled before the rework no longer build, and
debug builds of edk2 are not possible on these boards at all.

A serial console needs a UART, so make EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT depend on
DRIVERS_UART, and only select CONSOLE_SERIAL for debug builds when a
UART driver is available.

Fixes: commit b4917ed44d04 ("payloads/edk2: rework serial output configuration")

TEST=olddefconfig with KCONFIG_WERROR=1 fails for lenovo/w541 with
EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT or EDK2_DEBUG before this change and passes after
it. emulation/qemu-q35 and lenovo/t480 still get CONSOLE_SERIAL with
either option.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig b/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
index 68021bd60..f857f19bb 100644
--- a/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
+++ b/payloads/external/edk2/Kconfig
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ choice
 
 config EDK2_DEBUG
 	bool "Generate edk2 debug build"
-	select CONSOLE_SERIAL
+	select CONSOLE_SERIAL if DRIVERS_UART
 	help
 	  Generate a debug build. Select this if you want to enable serial debugging output.
 
@@ -261,6 +261,7 @@ config EDK2_SERIAL_SUPPORT
 	bool "Enable serial console"
 	default y if EDK2_DEBUG
 	default n
+	depends on DRIVERS_UART
 	depends on !EDK2_CBMEM_LOGGING
 	select CONSOLE_SERIAL
 	help
-- 
